l_name":"sase-op.1","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-op","agent_clan_generation":"20260817120415","approve":true,"bead_id":"sase-op.1","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-op[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]sase glossary command and on-demand glossary context[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Agents fetch glossary definitions on demand with `sase glossary [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]read <term>`, which prints the term plus the transitive closure of [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]terms its definition depends on and records an audited, visible [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]read; the always-loaded glossary memory note is gone, replaced by [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]one concise Tier 2 instruction block, so the glossary can grow [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]without growing every agent's context.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]6[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]glossary_command.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/glossary_command.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-op[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-op/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Glossary resolution core and read-log foundation[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core: add the shared term-reference lookup and recursive [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reference-closure resolver over the Rust glossary matcher, plus the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]glossary read-event model, JSONL store, and summaries; make the ACE [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]preview modal's cross-references delegate to the shared resolver.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Retire the generated glossary note for a Tier 2 instruction [/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]block[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]init[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]init: stop generating `sase/memory/glossary.md`, delete the previously [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]generated note, and render a `**GLOSSARY TERMS:**` block into the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]AGENTS.md Tier 2 section whenever a project configures glossary entries.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase glossary group with list and show[/bold #D7AFFF]                        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]cli[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli: register the `sase glossary` command group with project selection, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the filtered multi-format `list` subcommand, and the recursive `show` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]subcommand with its provenance-annotated rendering.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase glossary read and log[/bold #D7AFFF]                                    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]audit[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core, cli[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]audit: add the reason-requiring `read` wrapper that appends an audited [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]event before printing show output, and the `log` dashboard that [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]summarizes recorded reads by term, by agent, and by event.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]GLOSSARY lane in the agent metadata panel[/bold #D7AFFF]                     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]panel[dim] · [dim][/dim]after audit[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]panel: add the per-agent glossary-read loader and render a GLOSSARY [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sub-section in the SASE CONTEXT section of the agent metadata panel, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]showing each read's terms, related-term count, and reason.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Documentation, completion spec, and end-to-end sweep[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]docs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core, init, cli, audit, panel[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs: update the CLI, configuration, init, memory, and ACE documentation[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]for the new command and the retired note, regenerate the completion spec[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]snapshot, and run the exhaustive verification lane over the combined [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tree.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-op","llm_provider":"grok","model":"grok-4.6","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-op.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-450e89c130caafb255dad1ce0d62e24b","started_at":"2026-08-17T16:06:44.703737+00:00","state":"active"},{"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"48e91e17316a8fd2e0cb9e1a48db86b2dba362db597c1f588027d7449fdcc716","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-op.4/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"meta":{"digest":"66788392852645042adafe70c9eb8030f0737942f5bb6a849bf0e3943dc3b24c","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-op.4/meta.json","size_bytes":633},"prompt":{"digest":"43bb44c05e63032871917cace5dc9a084d2a13b2faaab7dab112258ab71b1b0c","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-op.4/prompt.md","size_bytes":170},"state":{"digest":"5589a00cbcb1097d3f9dd773b44f1842de353146bdfe93de9ebc8a42d003cef5","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-op.4/state.json","size_bytes":163}},"finished_at":null,"global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-op.4","local_name":"sase-op.4","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-op","agent_clan_gene